This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi Zero W to monitor a potted plant using a HiLetgo Soil Moisture Sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI. It reads the sensor data, calibrates it, logs the data to a file, and sends an email alert if the moisture level drops below a specified threshold. The program handles errors, logging, and graceful shutdown using signal handling and resource management.

