This C program uses the libgpiod library to access the SPI device and the GPIO pins for the MCP3008 ADC. It sets up the SPI device with the specified mode, speed, and bits per word, and configures the GPIO lines for SPI communication. The program reads analog data from the DFRobot Soil Moisture Sensor v2.0 connected to channel 0 of the MCP3008 via SPI, calculates the moisture percentage, and logs it to the console every 5 seconds. The program handles errors and releases resources on all exit paths, including signal handling for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

