This C program uses the libgpiod library to read analog data from a SEN0193 Capacitive Soil Moisture Sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC over SPI on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. The program sets up the SPI device, GPIO line, and performs a SPI transfer to read the ADC value. It then converts the ADC value to a moisture percentage and logs the reading to the console with a timestamp. The program handles errors and cleans up all resources on all exit paths, including SIGINT and SIGTERM.

