This C program uses the pigpio library to read analog data from a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI. It activates a 12V water pump when the moisture reading falls below a low threshold and turns it off when the reading rises above a high threshold with hysteresis. The program logs every moisture reading and every pump state change to an in-memory circular buffer and prints the full log buffer after each sample. It handles errors and gracefully exits on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

