This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor a Honeywell SS49E linear Hall-effect sensor connected to an ADS1115 ADC on I2C bus 1. It samples the sensor at 1 Hz, converts the raw voltage to magnetic field strength in Gauss, and stores the last 10 readings in a circular buffer. If the rolling average of the buffer exceeds a compile-time threshold, it immediately drives GPIO27 HIGH to signal motor shutdown and keeps it HIGH. The program logs all readings, threshold events, and errors via syslog. It handles pigpio initialization failure, I2C/ADC read failures, and invalid voltage readings outside 0-3.3 V. On SIGINT/SIGTERM, it stops the I2C handle, resets GPIO27 to LOW, terminates pigpio, and closes syslog.

