This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and SPI interfaces, sets up PWM for two vibration motors, and reads from an ADC to detect ambient noise. It logs events to a file and controls the motors based on the noise level. The program handles errors and gracefully shuts down on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

