This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and SPI interfaces, sets up a signal handler to gracefully shut down the program on SIGINT or SIGTERM, and reads analog values from a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI. It logs moisture readings to the console every 60 seconds and turns on a 12V water pump when the moisture drops below 30%. The program handles errors and retries failed SPI transfers up to 3 times.

