This C program uses the libgpiod library to control a camera pan-tilt system with two hobby servos on a Raspberry Pi. It handles button presses to increment or decrement the servo positions, clamped to the range [25, 125], and updates the PWM duty cycle accordingly. The program runs in an infinite loop, polling for button events and updating the servos every 50 ms. It also includes a signal handler to cleanly release all GPIO resources when the program is interrupted.

