This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the pigpio library to detect motion via an HC-SR501 PIR sensor connected to GPIO17. It captures a JPEG snapshot every 100 ms, applying a 2-second debounce after each motion event. The program sends a JSON payload containing the filename, an ISO 8601 timestamp with microseconds, the motion status, and the GPIO pin number to a specified server using libcurl. The program handles errors, checks all system calls, libcurl operations, and file operations, and provides clean shutdown on SIGINT and SIGTERM.

