This C program uses the pigpio library to control two SG90 servo motors connected to GPIO17 (pan) and GPIO18 (tilt) on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. It reads user input from stdin to adjust the pan and tilt angles in 5-degree increments, enforcing limits of 0 to 180 degrees. The program handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) and 'q' input to set both servos to the neutral position and terminate pigpio cleanly. It includes error handling for angle out-of-range and PWM failures, and a 100 ms delay between commands to prevent excessive CPU usage.

