This C program uses the libgpiod library to drive an HC-SR04 ultrasonic distance sensor for a proximity-based plant watering reminder. It generates a 10 microsecond trigger pulse, measures the echo pulse width using libgpiod edge events with CLOCK_MONOTONIC, and computes distance as (pulse_seconds * 34300) / 2 cm. The program checks every libgpiod call, applies a 30 ms timeout on each phase, treats an echo that never rises as sensor-absent and an echo stuck high as a timeout, and rejects readings outside 2-400 cm. It logs every measurement, including error and timeout entries, with an ISO-8601 timestamp to 'distance_log.txt', polling every 60 seconds. If the measured distance is below 15 cm, it logs a 'Time to water the plant!' reminder. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, releasing all libgpiod resources and closing the log file.

