This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to read data from an Adafruit APDS9960 sensor using the pigpio library. It continuously reads the RGB color values and proximity data, logging them to a CSV file when the proximity exceeds a threshold of 200. The program handles I2C communication errors by re-opening the bus and re-initializing the sensor, and it gracefully shuts down on receiving SIGINT or SIGTERM.

