This C program uses the pigpio library to interface with an Adafruit VL53L0X Time-of-Flight sensor over I2C bus 1 at its default address 0x29. It configures GPIO 17 (BCM numbering) with a pull-up and triggers a single distance measurement on each falling edge detected there. The program verifies sensor presence at 0x29 before initialization, writes 0x01 to SYSRANGE_START (register 0x00), polls bit 0 of RESULT_INTERRUPT_STATUS (register 0x13) until it sets, reads the 14-byte result block starting at RESULT_RANGE_STATUS (register 0x14) and extracts the 16-bit distance from bytes 10-11, and finally clears the interrupt by writing 0x01 to SYSTEM_INTERRUPT_CLEAR (register 0x0B). It logs each timestamped distance measurement, in millimetres, to 'distance_log.txt' in CSV format as 'timestamp,distance_mm'. The program handles robust error handling to every I2C transaction and to sensor-absent and timeout paths, and applies graceful shutdown on all exit paths.

