This C program initializes a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ with a MPR121 capacitive touch sensor and uses libgpiod to control four LEDs. It polls the touch status registers every 50 ms and triggers distinct 4-bit LED patterns based on which electrode detects proximity. The program logs all proximity events to a file and handles sensor-absent or bus-error paths gracefully. It also ensures clean resource release on all exit paths using signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM.

