This C program sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to interface with a Sensirion SHT40 humidity and temperature sensor using standard Linux I2C ioctls. It handles I2C open, ioctl, write, and read errors, validates every reading with the Sensirion CRC-8 algorithm, logs temperature and humidity readings with timestamps to 'sht40_log.txt' every 5 seconds, and robustly handles sensor absence or read failures by retrying on the next cycle. The program also cleans up resources on SIGINT (Ctrl+C) or SIGTERM.

