This C program initializes the pigpio library, opens the I2C bus, sets up signal handlers, and enters a loop to periodically trigger a measurement from the Sensirion SDP31 sensor. It reads the raw data, converts it to pressure and temperature, logs the data to a file, and handles I2C write and read failures with retry logic. The program exits cleanly on SIGINT or SIGTERM, closing the I2C handle, log file, and terminating pigpio resources.

