This C program uses the pigpio library to read temperature and humidity from a Silicon Labs Si7015 sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x40. It uses the No Hold Master mode to perform the measurements and logs each reading with a timestamp to 'sensor_data.txt' in append mode. The program handles transient I2C failures and exits cleanly on sensor-absent or bus-error conditions. It also handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) by closing the I2C handle, terminating pigpio, and closing any open file before exiting.

