This C program uses the pigpio library to interface with a Si7021 humidity and temperature sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x40. It controls a cooling fan on GPIO18 (active-high) and logs each reading with a timestamp into a 60-entry circular buffer. The program handles sensor-absent conditions, retry failed I2C transactions up to 3 times, and degrades gracefully. It also handles SIGINT cleanly by turning off the fan, closing the I2C handle, and calling `gpioTerminate()` before exiting.

