This C program uses the pigpio library to read temperature from an Analog Devices TMP05 digital temperature sensor connected to GPIO4. It measures the high pulse width (TH) and total cycle width (TL) via busy-wait polling with microsecond-level timing, using `gpioTick()` for timestamps. The reading is converted to degrees Celsius using the formula `Temperature = 4215 - (2143 * TH / TL)`. The program logs each valid reading with an ISO-8601 timestamp to 'temperature_log.txt' in append mode, sampling once every 5 seconds. It checks pigpio initialisation and file open results, detects sensor-absent or stuck-line conditions via a 50 ms timeout on each edge wait, guards against division by zero if TL is zero, flags readings outside the valid range -40 to +150 °C as errors, and after 3 consecutive failures, logs a 'SENSOR MALFUNCTION' entry to the log file. It handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for clean shutdown, closing the file and releasing pigpio.

