This C program uses the pigpio library to read differential pressure from a Honeywell Zephyr HAF Series HAFBLF0100A2AX5 digital airflow sensor over I2C bus 1 at 7-bit address 0x28. It drives a PWM fan on GPIO18 (a hardware-PWM-capable pin) at 25 kHz based on the computed flow rate. The sensor operates on the heat transfer principle and returns a 16-bit word whose 2 most significant bits are status bits; mask them off and shift the result right by 2 to obtain the 14-bit raw flow reading. Convert the 14-bit reading to flow rate using the linear transfer function where 1638 counts correspond to 0 SLPM and 14745 counts correspond to 10 SLPM. Scale the fan's PWM duty cycle linearly between 0% at 0 SLPM and 100% at 10 SLPM. Sample the sensor every 100 ms and log each reading with a timestamp to flow_log.txt in the comma-separated format "timestamp,pressure_Pa\n". Implement robust error handling for I2C communication failures, logging errors to stderr without crashing. Handle SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown: turn off the fan, close the I2C handle, flush and close the log file, and terminate pigpio.

