This C program reads temperature from an LM75 sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x48 using the libgpiod library. It reads the 16-bit temperature register (0x00) every 1 second, converts the raw value to degrees Celsius, logs each reading to an in-memory circular buffer with a capacity of 60 samples, computes the running average, and triggers an LED on GPIO 18 if the temperature exceeds 28.0°C. The program handles sensor-absent and bus-error paths by logging to stderr and attempting re-initialization, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths including SIGINT.

