This C program uses the pigpio library to control a solid-state relay on GPIO17, modulating a resistive heater to maintain a target temperature read from a MAX31855 thermocouple amplifier over the hardware SPI peripheral. It logs temperature and PWM duty cycle to `heater_log.csv` with ISO-8601 timestamps. The program implements a PI controller with anti-windup and a safe maximum duty cycle of 80% to prevent overheating. It handles SPI read failures or a MAX31855 fault by immediately setting the heater duty cycle to 0%, logging the error, and continuing running. The program also handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown, turning off the heater, closing SPI, closing the log file, and terminating pigpio.

