This C program uses the pigpio library to interact with the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B and the BMP180 pressure sensor. It sets up a falling-edge interrupt on GPIO4 to toggle logging on and off, debouncing the button press using pigpio tick comparison. The program reads the BMP180 calibration coefficients and validates them, then reads the pressure every 2 seconds when logging is enabled. The pressure readings are timestamped and logged to a file. The program handles SIGINT cleanly by closing the I2C handle and releasing pigpio resources before exiting.

