This C program uses the pigpio library to interface with two Sensirion SLF3S-1300F liquid flow sensors connected through a Sensirion SF06 multiplexer breakout. It continuously polls both sensors every 1 second, reads 3 bytes per sensor (2 data bytes plus 1 CRC byte), validates the CRC-8 checksum, and logs the flow rates to a comma-separated file named `flow_log.txt`. The program handles I2C errors robustly with up to 3 retries per sensor and implements clean shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

