This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor a SainSmart IR Flame Sensor Module connected to GPIO 4. It polls the sensor every 50 ms with software debouncing and logs events to 'flame_log.txt'. When a flame is detected, it drives a PWM-controlled cooling fan on GPIO 18 using hardware PWM at 100 Hz, scaling the duty cycle based on flame duration using an exponential curve. The program handles sensor-absent conditions with a timeout and cleanly releases all resources on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

