This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to detect the direction of rotation from two Melexis MLX90217 unipolar Hall-effect sensors connected to GPIO 17 and GPIO 27. It uses pigpio alerts for edge-triggered interrupts and a quadrature state machine to track the direction of rotation. The direction is logged to a file with a millisecond-precision timestamp. The program handles errors and uses a signal handler for graceful shutdown.

