This C program uses the pigpio library to monitor coolant flow in a miniature liquid cooling system with a Sensirion SLF3S-1300F liquid flow sensor on I2C bus 1. It sends a command to start continuous measurement, reads the raw flow value and CRC, validates the CRC, converts the raw value to ml/min, and logs the flow rate, raw sensor flags, and a computed status string to a comma-separated 'cooling_log.csv' file. The program handles I2C read failures, CRC failures, out-of-range flow rates, and graceful shutdown on SIGINT.

