This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using the pigpio library to read heart-rate data from a Silicon Labs Si1182-A-GM optical heart-rate sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x4A. It checks every return code, handles errors, and releases resources on all exit paths. The program logs valid heart-rate readings to a CSV file and retries on transient I2C read errors without crashing. It also handles SIGINT gracefully, closing the I2C handle, terminating pigpio, and closing the log file on all exit paths.

