This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and SPI interfaces, opens the BH1750 I2C sensors, and the APA102 LED strip. It reads the ambient light from the sensors, calculates the average lux, maps it to a brightness level, and fades the LED strip accordingly. The program handles sensor absence and I2C bus errors gracefully and uses a SIGINT signal handler to ensure clean resource release on exit.

