This C program uses the pigpio library to interface with the LSM303DLHC accelerometer on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It continuously reads the accelerometer data, calculates the total G-force magnitude, and logs impact events to a file when the G-force exceeds a configurable threshold. The program handles I2C read/write errors, sensor absence, and exits cleanly on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

