This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi's I2C bus and communicates with an LSM6DSR IMU to read accelerometer and gyroscope data. It logs the data in CSV format to a file named `motion_log.txt`. The program implements a basic fall-detection state machine using an acceleration-magnitude threshold. It handles I2C read/write errors, a sensor-absent condition via a WHO_AM_I check, and bus errors gracefully. The program also ensures clean resource release on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

