This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to read angular velocities from a GY-50 L3G4200D gyroscope using the pigpio library. It configures the sensor for normal mode with all axes enabled and +-250 dps full-scale range. The program reads all 6 data bytes starting at OUT_X_L in a single block read, converts raw values to degrees per second, and logs each sample with a nanosecond-precision timestamp to 'gyro_log.csv'. The program handles sensor-absent and bus-error paths, retries I2C writes up to 3 times during initialization, and uses signal handling for graceful termination.

