This C program initializes the Adafruit LIS3MDL magnetometer on a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ using the Linux i2c-dev ioctl interface. It configures the sensor for continuous-conversion mode at 80 Hz ODR with high-performance mode on all axes, reads the 6-byte little-endian X/Y/Z magnetic-field output registers, applies fixed offset/scale calibration constants, converts to milliGauss, and appends comma-separated X,Y,Z values to 'magnetic_log.txt' at 10 Hz. It checks every I2C read/write for errors and retries initialization up to 3 times. It handles SIGINT/SIGTERM cleanly by closing the I2C file descriptor and the log file. It also includes a simple metal-detector threshold alert printed to stderr when the total field magnitude exceeds 800 mG.

