This C program initializes the SPI device and a libgpiod line for the CS pin, configures the SPI device for SPI Mode 3, MSB first, and a 1 MHz clock speed. It then enables data ready mode in the ADIS16266 and periodically reads the X, Y, and Z angular rate output registers using the two-transfer read protocol. The raw 16-bit signed values are converted to angular rates using the scale factor of 0.02 deg/sec/LSB and logged to the console every 100 ms. The program includes robust error handling and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including SIGINT.

