This C program initializes a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using pigpio for I2C and hardware PWM to implement a theremin using an MPR121 capacitive touch sensor over I2C bus 1 at address 0x5A. The program acts as a TCP server listening on port 12345; when a client sends a message starting with 'MOTION_DETECTED:' and containing the shared secret 'MySecretKey', the theremin plays tones for 5 seconds based on capacitive touch readings, using hardware PWM on GPIO18. The program handles errors for pigpio initialization, I2C open/read, and socket/bind/listen/accept, and on SIGINT/SIGTERM, stops PWM, closes I2C and sockets, and terminates pigpio cleanly.

