This C program uses the pigpio library to interface with an HMC5883L magnetometer via I2C on bus 1 at address 0x1E. It configures the sensor for 8-sample averaging, 15 Hz output rate, and a gain setting of 1.3 Gauss. It continuously collects raw readings, computes hard-iron offsets as a running average over a 100-sample window, and applies these offsets to the latest raw reading to print the offset-corrected (not unit-normalized) X, Y, and Z values to stdout. The program handles I2C read/write errors on stderr and ensures clean resource release of the I2C handle and pigpio library on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

