This program initializes the LSM303D accelerometer, configures it for 50 Hz ODR with all axes enabled, and sets up an interrupt on the INT1 pin. It reads acceleration data at roughly 10 ms intervals and stores each sample in a circular buffer. On a rising edge of the INT1 GPIO interrupt, it prints a timestamp and dumps the last 10 buffered samples. The program handles initialization failures, runtime I2C read failures, and SIGINT gracefully.

