This C program uses the libgpiod API to read an SW-420 vibration sensor's active-high digital output on GPIO17. It polls for both rising and falling edges, logs each event with an ISO-8601 timestamp and the raw value (0 or 1), and implements a basic earthquake early-warning simulation by maintaining a sliding window of the last 5 events. If 3 or more of them read HIGH, it prints an EARTHQUAKE ALERT message to the console. The program handles errors gracefully and exits cleanly on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

