This C program uses the libgpiod library to control four 5V relay modules on the Raspberry Pi Zero W. It opens the gpiochip once and requests the four lines as outputs with an inactive drive of 1. Every 10 seconds, it generates a simulated soil-moisture value from 0 to 100 using rand(), seeded once at startup. If the moisture reading is below 30, it sequentially activates each relay for 5 seconds, then deactivates it, leaving a 1-second gap between relays. The activation events are logged with an ISO-8601 timestamp, relay number, and moisture level to irrigation_log.txt in append mode. The program checks every libgpiod call and file operation for errors, printing diagnostics to stderr. On SIGINT or SIGTERM, it deactivates all relays, releases the lines, closes the chip and the log file, and exits cleanly.

