This C program reads X, Y, and Z axis angular rates from an MPU-9250 gyroscope over SPI using the standard Linux spidev interface with libgpiod for chip-select control. It logs each reading with an ISO-8601 timestamp including nanoseconds to `gyro_log.txt` in CSV format. The program handles SPI communication errors up to 3 times, retries file write errors, and cleans up resources on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

