This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using the pigpio library to read tilt from an MPU-6050 accelerometer/gyroscope on I2C bus 1. It sets up the sensor, reads the accelerometer data every 100 ms, computes the roll and pitch, and turns on an LED if the tilt exceeds 45 degrees. The program logs each reading to a CSV file and prints the roll and pitch to the console. It handles SIGINT (Ctrl+C) to turn off the LED, close the I2C handle, and terminate pigpio, ensuring resource cleanup on all exit paths.

