This C program uses the pigpio library to read accelerometer data from an ADXL345 over I2C. It configures the sensor for ±2g range and full resolution, enables measurement mode, and reads the X, Y, and Z axis data every 100 ms. It detects a freefall event when all three axes have an absolute value below 0.2g for a continuous 0.5 seconds, simulating an alarm by driving GPIO27 high for 5 seconds, and logs each freefall event to a CSV file. The program handles I2C errors and uses a SIGINT handler to close resources and terminate pigpio.

