This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi 5 using the pigpio library to read acceleration data from an Adafruit LIS3DH accelerometer over I2C bus 1. It configures the accelerometer for a 100 Hz data rate and ±2g full scale, and continuously reads 16-bit signed acceleration values. It detects freefall and impact based on predefined thresholds and activates a buzzer for 1 second on impact. The program handles I2C communication failures with up to 3 retries, performs graceful cleanup on SIGINT, and ensures resources are released on every exit path.

