This C program uses the pigpio library to read acceleration data from an Adafruit LIS3DH accelerometer over I2C. It configures the sensor for ±2g range, high-resolution mode, and 100 Hz output data rate. The program reads acceleration at 10 Hz, computes g as the 16-bit signed raw value shifted right 4 bits, and scaled by 0.0009765625 (2g / 2048). If the absolute acceleration on any axis exceeds a user-defined threshold in g, it logs the event with timestamp and axis values to `/var/log/high_acceleration.log` and immediately triggers a system shutdown via `sudo shutdown -h now`. The program handles I2C open/configuration errors with cleanup and exit, handle sensor read errors gracefully by returning zeros and continuing, and validates the I2C address range and threshold from the command line. It also registers a SIGINT handler that closes I2C and terminates pigpio, and allows a graceful exit with code 0 when pigpio initialization or I2C open fails in a non-hardware environment.

