This C program initializes the Raspberry Pi's GPIO and I2C, sets up the BH1750 sensor to One-Time High-Resolution mode, and continuously reads the ambient light levels. It logs the readings to a file and activates a relay when the lux level falls below 150, deactivating it when the lux level is 150 or above. The program handles I2C communication errors, sensor absence, and bus errors by logging errors and retrying on the next cycle. It also includes signal handling for graceful termination on SIGINT and SIGTERM.

