This C program uses the pigpio library to control a 12V relay-connected LED strip based on ambient light read from a BH1750 sensor. It implements a hysteresis loop to prevent rapid toggling of the relay. The program logs all sensor readings and relay state changes to a file. It handles errors for pigpio initialization, I2C bus communication, and file I/O, and safely turns off the relay if the sensor fails to respond. The program also ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including graceful shutdown via SIGINT and SIGTERM.

