This C program uses the pigpio library to decode NEC IR remote signals from an IR receiver connected to GPIO17. It registers a pigpio alert callback to capture pulse timings, decodes the 32-bit NEC frame, validates the decoded command, logs the decoded address and command to syslog, and publishes each decoded command as JSON to an MQTT broker at localhost:1883 on topic `ir/decoded`. The program checks pigpio initialization, handles GPIO initialization failures, guards against pulse buffer overflow, validates the NEC checksum, and cleanly releases pigpio, MQTT, and syslog resources on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

