This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to read ambient light levels from four BH1750FVI sensors connected to the I2C-1 bus at 7-bit addresses 0x23, 0x24, 0x25, and 0x26. It uses the standard Linux I2C ioctl interface to communicate with the sensors and the UDP socket to broadcast the readings. The program handles errors and exits cleanly on SIGINT and SIGTERM.

