This C program interfaces with an Omron D7S seismic sensor over I2C using the Linux i2c-dev kernel interface. It reads the 6 bytes of tri-axial acceleration and converts them to g using the specified conversion factor. The program logs the data to a CSV file and errors to an error log file. It supports command-line options for setting the I2C address, interval, and output file. The program handles transient failures, sensor-absent, and bus-error conditions, and logs all errors with timestamps. It also supports graceful shutdown via SIGINT and SIGTERM.

