This C program initializes a BH1750 ambient light sensor on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B using the standard Linux I2C character-device API. It continuously reads the sensor's raw value, converts it to lux, and broadcasts the value as a floating-point string over UDP multicast to 239.255.255.250:5000 with TTL set to 1. The program handles errors and retries on I2C write and read operations, and on sensor absence or a bus error. It also uses a signal handler for SIGINT and SIGTERM to properly clean up the I2C file descriptor and socket on exit, and runs indefinitely using standard POSIX sockets until interrupted.

